Given the fact that the henchman (in previous suggestions, really) does
everything for money, why not give some depth to the most famous
moneylover in the dungeon: the leprechaun.
I suppose they can be tamed in 3.0, but behave not really different from
other tame creatures.
That can be changed. Make tame l's pick up everything (except for cursed
items, of course) and sell it to you. Of course, if you give them enough
food, their prices will be much lower. One item will always be for free
from a tame leprechaun: a magic whistle. As soon as he finds one, he'll
take it to you, just to make sure that his neverending source of income
has a chance not to leave him behind. Tamed l's do not fight
voluntarily, unless the monsters carry gold or valuable items. If you
and your pet arrive on a shop level, a fight breaks out between the pet
and the shopkeeper (the l robs the shop), but the shopkeeper can't win
if he doesn't hit hard enough the first time - although some shopkeepers
may have rings of teleport (control) in stock.
A rich tame leprechaun may retire in a room of its own (where did I hear that
before?) and call himself C******. An experienced leprechaun wouldn't be
of much use:
